      "side": 1,
      "message": "Seems like the only reason memory.h is used outside hyp code is because `arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm_constants.c` includes it.\n\nIf we want to get rid of it I can apply:\n\n```\n--- a/arch/x86/kvm/Makefile                                                    \n+++ b/arch/x86/kvm/Makefile                                                    \n@@ -53,6 +53,7 @@ pkvm-intel-$(CONFIG_PKVM_INTEL)       +\u003d ../../../drivers/iommu/intel/pkvm_iommu.o\n $(obj)/vmx/pkvm_init.o: $(obj)/pkvm_constants.h\n $(obj)/vmx/pkvm_host.o: $(obj)/pkvm_constants.h\n\n+CFLAGS_pkvm-constants.o   :\u003d -D__PKVM_HYP__\n $(obj)/pkvm-constants.s: $(src)/pkvm/pkvm_constants.c FORCE\n```\n\nand then remove `pkvm_sym` from memory.h",
