      "message": "We do panic dumps in a different way?\n\nAlso \"for jump_label/kprobe instruction decoding\" might sound puzzling, since it doesn\u0027t make it clear that this is not about kprobes for pKVM code itself (for which the host kernel is not expected to be able to install kprobes).\n\nMaybe e.g. \"Keep .pkvm.text mapped read-only, since it contains no secrets, while the host kernel may need to inspect pKVM text in some cases, e.g. for instruction decoding in arch_jump_entry_size() for getting size of a pKVM\u0027s static branch.\" ?",
