        "id": 3494485
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-16T03:43:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Following up on the `PKVM_PAGE_SHARED_BORROWED` comment above: instead of introducing `host_mmu_map_ro()` and special-casing `.pkvm.text` in `fix_host_mmu_pgstate_walker()`, could we simply skip `.pkvm.text` in the `host_mmu_unmap()` loop and call `pkvm_host_donate_hyp_share_ro(infos[i].pa, infos[i].size, false)` right after `fix_host_mmu_pgstate()` in `pkvm_host_mmu_init()`?",
      "revId": "651d8890f177e183a9727fdc9abd3607ef45f8ff",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "92535c0c_f098c32e",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/mmu.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 906,
      "author": {
        "id": 3484945
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-20T12:24:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it is better to keep it as is (+/- using PKVM_PAGE_SHARED_BORROWED which I\u0027ve applied) because:\n1) ed4a5fc728df (ANDROID: pKVM: x86: Don\u0027t use donation API during host MMU creation) deliberately stopped using runtime donation APIs during pkvm_host_mmu_init() (and 770acba366ee6 (\"ANDROID: pKVM: x86: Mark ramoops memory as shared-borrowed\") follows the same approach)\n2) Now after https://android-review.googlesource.com/q/topic:%22pkvm-v6.18-mmio-pgstate-cleanup%22 we get rid of fix_host_mmu_pgstate() and we only have verify_host_mmu_pgstate() which should be called at the end to verify - so we need to do all mapping before calling verify_host_mmu_pgstate() which we do in this commit.\n3) pkvm_host_donate_hyp_share_ro() uses host_mmu_pte_prot(false, false) which calls calc_pte_perm(true, write, true) and results in R\u003d1 W\u003d0 X\u003d1 permissions. BTW just wondering if setting X\u003d1 for all pkvm_host_donate_hyp_share_ro() is not a bug on its own (probably not harmful now but not so correct - maybe I will prepare separate patch with that outside of this patchset).\n4) using host_mmu_map_ro() here makes it symetrhinc to host_mmu_unmap() (both are matching low-level host_mmu_* init helpers and not mixing with higher-level runtime donate API).",
      "parentUuid": "60eecb22_8019a407",
      "revId": "651d8890f177e183a9727fdc9abd3607ef45f8ff",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
